r":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"ECON 501 - Business and Economic History","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":530.8212129171698,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":468.88,"t":537.94800537},"charspan":[0,40],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/45","text":"ECON 501 - Business and Economic History"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Credits: 4","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":519.8184779597921,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":345.85599983,"t":526.94800537},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/46","text":"Credits: 4"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"This course studies the historical influence of business enterprises on the development of capitalist economies, with an emphasis on the United States. Topics include the rise of manufacturing, development of financial institutions and markets, innovation and new markets, the role of the entrepreneur, and the impact of government policy on business development. Because this is an Inquiry course, each student will pursue a major research project. Does not satisfy Economics Major or Minor requirements. DISC: HP and INQ.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":431.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":571.9680000000001,"t":515.94800537},"charspan":[0,523],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/47","text":"This course studies the historical influence of business enterprises on the development of capitalist economies, with an emphasis on the United States. Topics include the rise of manufacturing, development of financial institutions and markets, innovation and new markets, the role of the entrepreneur, and the impact of government policy on business development. Because this is an Inquiry course, each student will pursue a major research project. Does not satisfy Economics Major or Minor requirements. DISC: HP and INQ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Attributes:","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/5"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":420.8212129171698,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":349.40799999999996,"t":427.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,11],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/48","text":"Attributes:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Historical Perspectives(Disc); Inquiry (Discovery)","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/5"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":420.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":349.40799941999995,"r":526.55999942,"t":427.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,50],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/49","text":"Historical Perspectives(Disc); Inquiry (Discovery)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Grade Mode:","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/5"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":409.8212129171698,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":357.08,"t":416.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,11],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/50","text":"Grade Mode:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Letter Grading","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/5"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":409.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":357.08000030999995,"r":410.28800031,"t":416.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/51","text":"Letter Grading"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"ECON 565 - Predictive Modeling: Data Driven Economic Analysis Credits: 4","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":383.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":542.5519999999999,"t":401.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,72],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/52","text":"ECON 565 - Predictive Modeling: Data Driven Economic Analysis Credits: 4"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"This course expands upon core topics in statistics through the study and practice of data management, data analysis, and statistical programming. Statistical programming and analytical skills are the key components of predictive modeling. Students will develop tools for collecting, organizing, interpreting, presenting, and analyzing business information. As an economics course an emphasis will be placed on how to use data to improve the information needed to make sound economic and business decisions based on marginal analysis.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":295.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":572.464,"t":379.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,533],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/53","text":"This course expands upon core topics in statistics through the study and practice of data management, data analysis, and statistical programming. Statistical programming and analytical skills are the key components of predictive modeling. Students will develop tools for collecting, organizing, interpreting, presenting, and analyzing business information. As an economics course an emphasis will be placed on how to use data to improve the information needed to make sound economic and business decisions based on marginal analysis."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Prerequisite(s): (ADMN 420 with a minimum grade of C- or ADMN 510 with a minimum grade of C-) and (ECON 402 with a minimum grade of Cor ECON 402H with a minimum grade of C- or EREC 411 with a minimum grade of C-).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":251.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":570.0160000000001,"t":291.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,213],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/54","text":"Prerequisite(s): (ADMN 420 with a minimum grade of C- or ADMN 510 with a minimum grade of C-) and (ECON 402 with a minimum grade of Cor ECON 402H with a minimum grade of C- or EREC 411 with a minimum grade of C-)."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Grade Mode:","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/6"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":240.82121291716976,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":357.08,"t":247.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,11],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/55","text":"Grade Mode:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Letter Grading","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/6"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":240.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":357.08000030999995,"r":410.28800031,"t":247.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/56","text":"Letter Grading"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"ECON 605 - Intermediate Microeconomic Analysis","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/6"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":225.82121291716976,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":491.04799999999994,"t":232.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,46],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/57","text":"ECON 605 - Intermediate Microeconomic Analysis"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Credits: 4","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":214.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":345.85599983,"t":221.94800537000003},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/58","text":"Credits: 4"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Analysis of supply and demand. Determination of prices, production, and the distribution of income in noncompetitive situations and in the purely competitive model. General equilibrium.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":181.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.4,"r":571.5440000000001,"t":210.94800536999992},"charspan":[0,185],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/59","text":"Analysis of supply and demand. Determination of prices, production, and the distribution of income in noncompetitive situations and in the purely competitive model. General equilibrium."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Prerequisite(s): (ECON 402 with a minimum grade of C- or ECON 402H with a minimum grade of C- or EREC 411 with a minimum grade of C-).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":159.81847795979206,"coord_origin":"BOTT